KRN-041: no-Apple-SoC-library export profile for arm64 machines without the KDK library

Base: apple-oss-distributions/xnu c54f35ca767986246321eb901baf8f5ff7923f6a
(xnu-8796.121.2), config/Private.arm64.exports. License: APSL 2.0, as the
file it changes. Author: KRN-041 (claude-export-dossier-20261110-x41).

Opt-in profile, for E1S and the BCM2837-based guest only. Never apply it to
T6000, T8101 or VMAPPLE: makedefs/MakeInc.def force-loads Apple's closed
lib<MACHINE>.os.<CONFIG>.a for those machines, and these names are expected
to come from it there.

It removes the 35 names that public source neither declares nor defines:
7 pmap_iommu_*, 11 DART/SART/UAT/NVMe PPL descriptor entry points and the 17
IOUnifiedAddressTranslator class symbols. They are kext-facing KPI: no object
or library of the linked kernel references any of them (KRN-041 scan), and the
project, HakiOS and S24-port driver sources do not either. Without a provider
the genuine check_all_exports and the Private symbol set fail on them. The
other two missing names, _pmap_has_iofilter_protected_write and
_pmap_cs_configuration, stay listed; 0001 defines them.

The removed lines are the same 35 that the S24 port's legacy
xnu/legacy-sweet-patches/0009-sweet-drop-apple-soc-only-exports.patch
(c8860decc62c6d6180e609036d027a2997972420) removes from this file.

